From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: orangepi-zero2: describe PL bank and
 SPI NOR supplies

The R_PIO pinctrl driver requests a "vcc-pl" supply for the PL bank
(RSB bus to the AXP305) and the SPI NOR core requests a "vcc" supply
for the flash. Neither is described for the Orange Pi Zero2, so both
drivers fall back to the dummy regulator and log at boot:

  sun50i-h616-r-pinctrl 7022000.pinctrl: supply vcc-pl not found, using dummy regulator
  spi-nor spi0.0: supply vcc not found, using dummy regulator

According to the Orange Pi Zero2 v1.3 schematic (power tree on the
AXP305 sheet) ALDO1 generates the 3.3V VCC-IO rail, which also sources
VCC-PC/PF/PH/PI already described here. The H616 has no separate PL
supply pin: PL0/PL1 (RSB_SCK/RSB_SDA) sit in the VCC-IO domain, so
the PL bank is powered by ALDO1 as well. The 2MiB SPI NOR flash hangs
off SPI0 on the PC bank and is powered from the same 3.3V rail.

Wire both supplies to ALDO1 ("vcc-sys"). ALDO1 is always-on, so this
is purely descriptive and does not change the power sequencing.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616-orangepi-zero2.dts
@@ -38,6 +38,14 @@
 	vmmc-supply = <&reg_dcdce>;
 };
 
+&r_pio {
+	/*
+	 * The PL bank (RSB to the PMIC) is in the H616's VCC-IO domain, which
+	 * the schematic shows is fed by ALDO1 (3.3V, "vcc-sys").
+	 */
+	vcc-pl-supply = <&reg_aldo1>;
+};
+
 &r_rsb {
 	status = "okay";
 
@@ -153,3 +161,9 @@
 	vcc-ph-supply = <&reg_aldo1>;
 	vcc-pi-supply = <&reg_aldo1>;
 };
+
+&spi0 {
+	flash@0 {
+		vcc-supply = <&reg_aldo1>;
+	};
+};
